 "text": "Southern Californians are again bracing for gusty winds and a heightened risk of wildfires less than two weeks after the start of deadly blazes that have killed at least 27 people and destroyed thousands of homes. The U.S. National Weather Service has issued a red flag warning signaling increased fire danger for Los Angeles on Monday and Tuesday due to low humidity and warm, dry Santa Ana winds.",
